<p>Note: On May 23 1997 Norfolk and CSX Corp through a jointly-owned entity completed the acquisition of Conrail Inc. Norfolk's share of the purchase price to acquire Conrail stock is expected to total $5.8 billion (including fees).</p>
<p>Financial highlights exclude the effects of Conrail-related items that reduced second-quarter net income by $10.7 million, or $0.09 per share, and reduced six-month Net income by $62.6 million, or $0.50 per share.</p>
<p>Including Conrail-related items, Net income for the second quarter was $190.1 million, or $1.52 per share, and for the first six months was $317.9 million, or $2.54 per share.</p>
<p>The items primarily reflect expenses associated with the acquisition of Conrail stock, such as interest expense on debt and credit facility costs, including the first-quarter pretax charge of $77.2 million, and &quot;Equity in earnings of Conrail.&quot; The latter, amounting to $22.9 million, represents NS' portion of Conrail's earnings, exclusive of items considered in purchase accounting.</p>
<p>Source:  Norfolk Southern Corp</p>
